# The HUD's health readouts - Vibe, EKF, the pre-arm line - drawn as HUD.cs draws them.
#
# The facts are read from the scene the display paints: each readout's colour by the C#'s brush
# name (white, orange, red), the pre-arm text, whether the red CPU is up, and whether the
# angle-of-attack elements showed. Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760, disarmed, sitting on
# the ground and past its start-up: GPS locked and the EKF settled, which takes SITL about half a
# minute from launch. The thresholds and every colour are in hud.rs's unit tests; this proves the
# live values reach them.

screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 2

# A copter at rest in SITL shakes far below the C#'s 30 m/s² line (HUD.cs:3168).
expect hud.vibe.colour white
# The red CPU is up only at a SYS_STATUS.load of exactly 1000, a full 100% (HUD.cs:3208,
# CurrentState.cs:2949). A copter at rest in SITL reports far less - the copter recording in
# testdata/mavlink/autotest.tlog reports 0 throughout - so it is down.
expect hud.cpu false
# A settled SITL EKF has attitude and horizontal velocity and variances near zero, so ekfstatus
# is under the C#'s 0.5 (HUD.cs:3228).
expect hud.ekf.colour white
# Disarmed, so the pre-arm line is up (HUD.cs:3266). SITL passes its pre-arm checks once the
# EKF and GPS are ready, which is white "Ready to Arm".
expect hud.prearm Ready to Arm
expect hud.prearm.colour white
# No editor for the user's extra fields and no stored list, so none are drawn.
expect hud.custom.count 0
# The flight path vector and the AOA scale are live, from AOA_SSA and AOA_CRIT, but show only
# once the vehicle sends an angle that is not 0 (displayAOASSA, HUD.cs:889-930). SITL's copter
# sends no AOA_SSA - there is none in testdata/mavlink/autotest.tlog - so neither shows here;
# hud.rs's unit tests drive them through an AOA_SSA message.
expect hud.fpv.shown false
expect hud.aoa.shown false
